-- title:
--   Substitution t ↦ t^q carries the Γ₀(qM') field into `fieldBar`
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. Let $g$ be a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying in `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma0 (q * M')))`, that is, in the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((t))$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise images, under the map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, of the elements of the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((t))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g$, taken over all weights $k$, all modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_0(qM')$ whose $q$-expansions are the integral power series $p_f$, $p_g$ respectively, with $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g \neq 0$. The conclusion is that the image of $g$ under `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`, the ring homomorphism multiplying every exponent by $q$ (classically the substitution $t \mapsto t^q$), lies in `fieldBar q M'`: the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   This is the degeneracy map $z \mapsto qz$ read on $q$-expansions at $\infty$: it realises the function field of $X_0(qM')$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ inside the function field of the relevant geometric component of level $q^2M'$ with the congruence condition modulo $q$. It feeds the statements on adjoining the image of `qExpand` to `fieldBar` and bounding the resulting relative degree, used in the full-level Jacobian construction.
